# GH-256: `forjar dist` output. Release builds it into /tmp/dist-output; a copy
# committed at the repo root in March went stale against the maintained
# install.sh and carried 7 bashrs SEC findings the real one does not.
/dist-output/
.dogfood/
.pv/

# pmat writes a `.pmat/` cache wherever it is INVOKED, not just at the repo
# root. A run from src/verb/ or tests/ leaves a nested one holding tdg-*.db
# scratch; on 2026-08-23 a `git add -A src/` staged eight of them.
#
# Unanchored so it catches every depth, which also covers the root — that is
# deliberate. The root `.pmat/` files the ratchets read (baseline.json,
# cb200-baseline.json, context.db) are already TRACKED, and gitignore never
# affects a tracked file, so they keep working. What this stops is a NEW cache
# artefact drifting into a commit from either place. Adding a genuinely new
# tracked file under .pmat/ needs `git add -f`, which is the right amount of
# friction for a directory that is otherwise all scratch.
**/.pmat/

# ── Derived pmat/pv caches (forjar#287) ─────────────────────────────────────
# These are regenerated from the source tree on demand. Tracking them meant the
# working tree was NEVER clean: every commit rewrote them, every rebase
# conflicted on them, and `.pmat/baseline.json` alone churns ~3700 lines per
# commit.
#
# Measured cost during the 2026-08-25 defect sweep: five rebases blocked, two
# `git checkout` calls silently refused (their error swallowed by a `2>/dev/null`
# that made the failure look like success), and one branch left mid-rebase for
# several operations because of it.
#
# `.pmat/context.db-shm` and `-wal` are SQLite journal sidecars — tracking a live
# database's write-ahead log in git cannot be right under any policy.
#
# NOT ignored, deliberately: baseline.json, cb200-baseline.json,
# file-health-baseline.json, metrics/dependencies.json and project.toml. The
# pre-commit hook reads baseline.json as a quality RATCHET, so it needs a shared
# starting point rather than one generated from whatever the local tree happens
# to be. Churny, and load-bearing — a separate decision from this one.
.pmat/context.db
.pmat/context.db-shm
.pmat/context.db-wal
.pmat/context.idx/
.pmat/workspace.db
.pmat/workspace.idx/
.pmat/dead-code-cache.json
.pmat/deny-cache.txt
.pmat/deps-cache.json
.pmat/lint-cache.txt
.pmat/hooks-cache/
.pv/lint-previous.json
